{
	"note": "Realistic animal models (Dave 6 Nov 2026: aim for photorealism; design/realistic_animals_plan.md, src/client/animal_view.gd _make_model). A species row here whose scene exists is drawn from that rigged, animated scene instead of the code-built body; no row or a missing file keeps the code body. Row: scene (res:// path of a .glb/.fbx/.tscn), scale, yaw_deg (turn so the animal faces -Z), walk_mps and run_mps (ground speeds the walk and run clips were made at), stride_m (metres per footstep), clips {state number or 'walk'/'run': clip name}; states 0 graze, 1 hop, 2 flee, 3 alert, 10 warn, 11 charge, 12 recover. Example: \"bear\": {\"scene\": \"res://assets/animals/bear/bear.glb\", \"scale\": 1.0, \"yaw_deg\": 180, \"walk_mps\": 1.3, \"run_mps\": 9.0, \"stride_m\": 1.1, \"clips\": {\"0\": \"Eat\", \"3\": \"Idle\", \"10\": \"Roar\", \"11\": \"Run\", \"12\": \"Idle\", \"walk\": \"Walk\", \"run\": \"Run\"}}. clip_prefix (optional) is put before every clip name; without it a clip is found by its name after the armature ('Armature|Idle' answers 'Idle'). The model files are bought (WildMesh 3D Ultimate 3D Animal Pack, Dave 6 Nov 2026) and are NOT in git (/assets/animals/ is ignored): copy them from the pack into assets/animals/<kind>/ on a build machine. length_m: the model is scaled so its longest side is this long (any file units). materials: [{match, albedo} or {match, hide: true}] colour textures set in code, first matching entry per surface (match '' = the rest). length_m values: design/wildmesh_scale_table.md (real adult length, nose to tail tip). Species added 7 Nov (deer, moose, boar, wolf, fox, rabbit): yaw, clip speeds and material matches are first guesses from the bear; the shot runner --shot-animals row checks them. pack (optional): the model's folder inside the bought pack; tools/install_animal_models.py copies it into the scene's folder (no .blend: headless import cannot read it). size_clip (optional): size and ground the model by its bones in that clip's first frame, for a file whose imported pose is not standing. bounds: mesh sizes by the skinned mesh instead of the bones. young_model (optional): a young animal of this species is drawn from this model at its own size (keys laid over the row like a variant) instead of the adult shrunk to half.",
